{"meta": {"limit": 500, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 8}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   To enable accounting and auditing in http\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2023-12-12T16:27:36Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1027/", "id": 117047, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-pradeepkumarxplorer-audit", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 3, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-pradeepkumarxplorer-audit/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/"], "std_level": null, "stream": null, "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/134148/"], "tags": [], "time": "2023-12-12T08:14:26Z", "title": "Internet Wall", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document defines the format of data to be collected and minimum set of attributes that need to be captured for security auditing in healthcare application systems.  The format is defined as an XML schema, which is intended as a reference for healthcare standards developers and application designers.  It consolidates several previous documents on security auditing of healthcare data.  This memo provides information for the Internet community.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/110104/", "expires": "2004-12-26T08:00:10Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1008/", "id": 27050, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-marshall-security-audit", "note": "", "notify": "rfc-editor@rfc-editor.org", "pages": 47, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-marshall-security-audit/", "rev": "12", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/inf/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ise/", "submissions": [], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/app-min/", "/api/v1/name/doctagname/via-rfc/"], "time": "2015-10-14T20:50:40Z", "title": "Security Audit and Access Accountability Message XML Data Definitions for Healthcare Applications", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 9483}, {"abstract": "This document defines an LDAP auxiliary object class and a single \r\nattribute, which together can be used to store and track the \r\nentities who may have accessed or modified a specific entry in an \r\nLDAP directory information tree. For example, an LDAP application \r\nmay need to store information which can indicate when an entry was \r\ncreated, when it was accessed, who modified it, and other kinds of \r\nsimilar information, with this information acting as a general-\r\npurpose auditing log for that entry. \r\nThe object class and attributes defined herein are designed for that \r\npurpose in particular, and are not intended to serve as detailed \r\nauditing information capable of withstanding court-of-law scrutiny, \r\nnor are they designed to be used for journaling-playback purposes. \r\nThey are simply to be used for storing general information about the \r\nchanges which have been made to a specific entry. ", "ad": null, "expires": "2003-10-02T07:00:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1027/", "id": 27524, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-hall-ldap-audit", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 0, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-hall-ldap-audit/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/"], "std_level": null, "stream": null, "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2003-03-31T08:00:00Z", "title": "The generalizedAudit object class and \r\nthe generalizedAuditEvent attribute", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1566}, {"abstract": "   Congestion Exposure (ConEx) is a mechanism by which senders inform\r\n   the network about the congestion encountered by previous packets on\r\n   the same flow.  Reliable auditing is necessary to provide a strong\r\n   incentive to declare ConEx information honestly.  This document\r\n   defines how the signals are handled by an audit and lists\r\n   requirements for an audit implementation.  This document does not\r\n   mandate a particular design but identifies state and functions that\r\n   any auditor element must provide to fulfill the requirements stated\r\n   in [draft-ietf-conex-abstract-mech].\r\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2016-10-16T18:22:04Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1027/", "id": 52303, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-wagner-conex-audit", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-wagner-conex-audit/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/"], "std_level": null, "stream": null, "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/55279/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/58196/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/77542/"], "tags": [], "time": "2016-10-16T07:06:20Z", "title": "Auditing of Congestion Exposure (ConEx) signals", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 2938}, {"abstract": "   This specification is an effort to provide guidelines for\n   implementing the Audit functionality for OAuth 2.0 enabled\n   environments.  The data of interest for the OAuth 2.0 audit includes\n   permissions, scopes, policies and other authorization and\n   authentication related information.  It can be used by user agents\n   and authorization services for fast violation response, credential\n   revocation, or by government agencies and various institutions for\n   forensic analysis.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2015-04-17T13:13:06Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1027/", "id": 55344, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-tsitkov-audit", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-tsitkov-audit/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/"], "std_level": null, "stream": null, "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/63544/"], "tags": [], "time": "2015-04-17T07:08:24Z", "title": "Audit in OAuth 2.0", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1727}, {"abstract": "   This specification is an effort to provide guidelines for\n   implementing the Audit functionality for OAuth 2.0 enabled\n   environments.  The data of interest for the OAuth 2.0 audit includes\n   scopes, permissions, policies and other authorization and\n   authentication related information.  It can be used by resource and\n   authorization servers for detecting security-related problems in real\n   time and fast violation response, or by government agencies and\n   various institutions for after-the-fact forensic and compliance\n   analysis.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2015-07-27T18:44:26Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1027/", "id": 58630, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-tsitkov-oauth-audit", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-tsitkov-oauth-audit/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/"], "std_level": null, "stream": null, "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/64908/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/65244/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/66142/"], "tags": [], "time": "2015-07-27T07:08:18Z", "title": "Audit in OAuth 2.0", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1974}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a tamper-evident audit chain for the\n   reasoning and actions of a Non-Human Entity (NHE).  Each audited\n   event --- a reasoning step obtained at the boundary to a model\n   provider, or a tool invocation obtained at the execution boundary ---\n   is recorded as an entry whose bound fields are hash-linked to its\n   predecessor, so that any alteration, omission, or reordering is\n   detectable by an independent verifier.  The chain binds metadata\n   (model, provider, subject identity, and reasoning scale) into the\n   entry hash, and supports a prove-without-exposing mode in which a\n   verifier confirms that an event occurred, with the attested metadata,\n   without the event's content being disclosed.  Content storage is\n   optional and its retention is configurable independently of the\n   chain, so content may be redacted without destroying the chain's\n   integrity.  The entry data model and canonical serialization are\n   specified here; the wire and proof-export encodings are deferred to\n   the next revision.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2027-02-14T17:15:05Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1027/", "id": 160398, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ruvalcaba-nhe-audit", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ruvalcaba-nhe-audit/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/"], "std_level": null, "stream": null, "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/167701/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-08-13T17:15:05Z", "title": "NHE Reasoning-Audit Log: A Tamper-Evident, Content-Optional Audit Chain for Autonomous Agents", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document describes PALA-1 -- version 1 of the Portable Append-\n   only Log for Audit -- a compact binary record format for tamper-\n   evident audit trails produced by AI inference runtimes and robotic\n   control systems.  It is designed for a class of deployment defined by\n   three constraints that hold together: the hardware is computationally\n   modest and its cycles are reserved for the workload and the power\n   budget rather than for the audit trail; no external witness is\n   reachable, whether because policy forbids outbound contact or because\n   the platform operates beyond connectivity, so a witness is\n   unavailable by rule or by physics rather than by circumstance; and\n   the right to verify the trail is separated from the right to read\n   what it records.\n\n   Records form an append-only hash chain.  Integrity verification\n   requires no key material of any kind, inspects no record bodies, and\n   costs one hash per record rather than one signature.  The format\n   distinguishes three separately answerable questions -- internal\n   consistency, completeness against an external anchor, and existence\n   at a point in time against an external witness -- and states which of\n   the three a given trail actually supports rather than implying all\n   three.\n\n   The format is frozen at version 1.0 and is described here as it is.\n   This document presents an existing wire format; it does not revise\n   one.  Where a deployment does permit an external witness, a chain\n   head may be published to a transparency service such as that of the\n   Supply Chain Integrity, Transparency, and Trust architecture (SCITT,\n   RFC 9943); that path is described but is not part of the hashing\n   contract.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2027-04-25T11:33:13Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1027/", "id": 160879, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-sparysh-pala-audit", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 44, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-sparysh-pala-audit/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/"], "std_level": null, "stream": null, "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/168508/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/169799/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/170740/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-10-22T11:33:14Z", "title": "PALA-1: A Tamper-Evident Audit Record Format for Constrained and Disconnected Deployments", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}]}